      "title": "Resources for",
      "description": "Faculty & Staff | Presbyterian College Skip to content Resources For Close Menu Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends First-Gen Students Community Apply Info Visit Give Open\r\n                            Search Search for: Open Apply Info Visit Give Search for: Admissions Admissions Why PC First-Year Students Transfer Students International Students Admitted Students Graduate Students Visit Us Academics Academics at PC Majors, Minors, & Special Programs Academic Resources Civil Conversations Heart of Service Center for Inquiry, Research & Scholarship Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Student Life Student Life Get Involved Health & Wellness Living on Campus Spiritual Life Career & Professional Development Blue Hose Athletics Cost & Aid Cost & Aid Affordability Scholarships Grants Loans FAFSA Net Price Calculator Student Employment Tuition & Fees Veteran Benefits About PC About Presbyterian College Leadership History, Mission & Plan Justice & Community Wellbeing For The Community Governance & Policies Accreditation Offices & Services News Giving Events FAQs Athletics Directory Alumni Resources For Close Menu Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends First-Gen Students Community Resources for Faculty & Staff Report Website Issues or Corrections Welcome to the Faculty & Staff Hub This is your go-to place for everything you need – with quick access to essential links and forms. We’ve organized it all to make your life a little easier. Quicklinks Bannerweb Brightspace Directory All offices All Forms IT Helpdesk email Single-sign on Student Cares form Registrar Academic Resources Academic Advising Academic Calendar Academic Success Coursera Course Catalog Course Offerings by Term Final Exams Library Provost Faculty Resources Student CARES Form Student Employment Checklists: – Supervisor Checklist – Student Checklist The Blue Book The Garnet Book Marketing & Communications Branding Guide Directory Profile Update Good News Marketing Services Ticket Newsletter Submission Report a Website Issue Submit an Event Form Health & Wellness Counseling Center Health Services Springs Student Center Student CARES Form Title IX Reporting Victim Support Campus Resources Accessible Education Campus Safety Campus Services Facility Rentals IT Helpdesk Mail Center Maintenance Request Human Resources A&S Faculty Handbook Bias Incident Reporting Employee Resources Personnel Handbook Title IX Reporting Other Resources Career & Prof. Development Resources for Faculty Russell Internship Program Governance & Policies Student Employment Checklists: – Supervisor Checklist – Student Checklist Holiday Schedule Fall 2026 Friday, July 3 Independence Day Monday, September 7 Labor Day Monday, October 12 Fall Break Wed-Fri, November 25-27 Thanksgiving Break* Mon-Thu, December 21-31 Christmas Break* Spring 2027 Fri, January 1 New Year’s Day Monday, January 18 Martin Luther King Day Friday, March 26 Good Friday Monday, May 31 Memorial Day Friday, June 18 Juneteenth Day More Holiday Info The Personnel Handbook recognizes certain holidays each academic year for full time staff employees. Some, but not all employees who have classifications other than full time will also receive the official paid days. Supervisors and employees should read the Personnel Handbook for staff’s eligibility to receive paid holidays. Please contact the Human Resource Office should you need additional information. The President and her Cabinet are pleased to announce that the 2026-2027 academic year holiday schedule will include extended days at Thanksgiving and Christmas. These extended days are for full time employees only. This larger block of holiday time will be determined each year by the President and the Leadership Team and should not be assumed to be an annual benefit. *Some full-time staff members will be required to work certain days during the extended holiday schedule, to cover essential duties , but they and their supervisor may, by prior agreement, substitute other days off so that each full-time staff member receives the same allotment of paid holidays. The substituted time off may not be extended into the next fiscal year nor may it be paid or taken at the rate of time and a half. Need Maintenance Assistance? Our team handles many general facility maintenance services, such as air conditioning repairs, office moves, custodial services, and more. Please submit all requests through our online portal to ensure prompt attention and proper tracking. This helps us prioritize your needs and keep you updated on the status of your request. Maintenance Request Forms & Guides Faculty & Staff Forms A&S Faculty Handbook PCSP Faculty Handbook Personnel Handbook Governance & Policies Campus Offices Check out our quick list or browse all offices Business Office Counseling Services Health Services Employment & HR Office of the Provost Campus Safety Justice & Community Wellbeing Marketing & Communications Registrar Bookstore Library Mail Center Scotsman’s Corner All Offices JUstice & Community Wellbeing At Presbyterian College, we strive to create a just campus where everyone can thrive by ensuring all voices are heard, experiences are valued, and journeys are supported as Blue Hose. Through celebrating our differences, we strengthen our academic excellence and prepare students to lead with justice in the diverse, interconnected world they will serve. Accessible Education Bias Incident Reporting Title IX Empowering First-Generation Students Presby First+ empowers first-generation college students through mentoring, resources, and a strong sense of community from day one. Presby First + Presby First+ Resources Email Signatures Showcase your first-gen pride and help promote the PresbyFirst+ program by adding our logo to your email signature. “I am PresbyFirst+” Email Signature You can copy/download the logo below: PresbyFirst+ Advocate Email Signature You can copy/download the logo below: Books & Materials Explore the Center for First-Generation Student Success —the leading source for research, resources, and professional development aimed at advancing first-gen student success in higher education. Discover evidence-based practices, learn from the latest national data, and access tools to better understand and support the unique experiences of first-generation students. Whether you’re seeking proven strategies or new insights, this site is your go-to hub for transforming the academic journey of first-gen learners. Upcoming Events Sep 24 NetVUE Regional Gathering Oct 29 Homecoming Friends and Family Weekend Planning an Event? Student organizations, faculty, and staff should submit the following form to register events hosted on or off-campus. Submit your form at least one week before your event date to avoid denial of your request. All registered events will be reviewed and may be added to the campus calendar. Event organizers and attendees must comply with Presbyterian College’s Honor Code and Garnet Book policies , as well as all federal, state, and local laws and organizational procedures. Contact the Office of Student Involvement at [email protected] with questions. Submit an Event Recent News View all News From PC to DC: Landon Norizsan ‘24 finds his calling in Washington media The Day It Rained in Belize: OT students discover important lessons outside the classroom PC opens 147th academic year with message of calling, community and courage New PC students begin college experience through service PC welcomes Class of 2030, transfer students to campus Presbyterian College’s Class of 2026 launches into careers, graduate study, entrepreneurship, and service PC names Rhonda Mingo Dean of Students PC School of Pharmacy welcomes Class of 2030 at White Coat Ceremony Resources For Close Menu Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends First-Gen Students Community Search for: 503 South Broad Street Clinton, South Carolina 29325 800.476.7272 Contact Us facebook instagram x flickr Quick Links & Resources Quick Links & Resources News Events Directory Athletics Campus Map Living on Campus Academic Calendar Course Catalog Offices & Facilities Accreditation Job Opportunities Justice & Community Wellbeing First-Gen Students International Students Accessible Education Health & Wellness Single-Sign On BannerWeb Brightspace Campus Bookstore Library Online Payment Resources For Close Menu Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends First-Gen Students Community Search for: © Copyright 2026 Presbyterian College | Title IX Policies Consumer Information Campus Police Presbyterian College is committed to providing an accessible and inclusive online experience. If you are unable to access any part of this website due to a disability, please contact Accessible Education at [email protected] for assistance. NOTICE OF NONDISCRIMINATORY POLICY AS TO STUDENTS: Presbyterian College is an equal educational opportunity institution. The College’s admission standards and practices are free from discrimination on the basis of age, sex, race, creed, color, disability, ethnicity or national origin. Apply Info Visit Give Search for: Resources For Close Menu Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends First-Gen Students Community"
