    "https://www.presby.edu/about/offices-and-services/human-resources/employment/financial-aid-counselor/": {
      "title": "Financial Aid Counselor",
      "description": "Financial Aid Counselor | Presbyterian College Press Option+1 for screen-reader mode, Option+0 to cancel Accessibility Screen-Reader Guide, Feedback, and Issue Reporting | New window Skip to content Resources For Close Menu Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends First-Gen Students Community Apply Info Visit Give Open\n                            Search Search for: Open Apply Info Visit Give Search for: Admissions Admissions Admissions Why PC First-Year Students Transfer Students International Students Admitted Students Graduate Students Visit Us Academics Academics Academics at PC Majors, Minors, & Special Programs Academic Resources Civil Conversations Heart of Service Center for Inquiry, Research & Scholarship Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Student Life Student Life Student Life Get Involved Health & Wellness Living on Campus Spiritual Life Career & Professional Development Blue Hose Athletics Cost & Aid Cost & Aid Cost & Aid Affordability Scholarships Grants Loans FAFSA Net Price Calculator Student Employment Tuition & Fees Veteran Benefits About PC About PC About Presbyterian College Leadership History, Mission & Plan Justice & Community Wellbeing For The Community Governance & Policies Accreditation Offices & Services News Giving Events FAQs Athletics Directory Alumni Resources For Close Menu Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends First-Gen Students Community Financial Aid Counselor Financial Aid Counselor About PC Offices & Services Human Resources Employment Financial Aid Counselor Financial Aid Counselor Position Summary The main purpose of this position is to oversee the daily operations of the office that include processing downloads from the Student Aid Internet Gateway (SAIG) mailbox, reviewing verification files, and reconciling Title IV aid. This position also meets and works closely with future and current families. Essential Job Functions Responsible for importing and exporting files through SAIG mailbox daily Process and review daily ISIRs Responsible for ensuring institutional compliance of all state, federal and alternative loan programs for Undergraduate students Responsible for the origination of federal loans through COD and Banner – to include Subsidized, Unsubsidized, Parent Plus Responsible for the certification of alternative loans on ELM and SC Student loans to include the SC Teacher Loan on the South Carolina Student Loan Corporation website Monitor the disbursements of state, federal and alternative loan funds for Undergraduate students Resolve loan issues concerning state, federal and alternative loans Reconcile all federal and alternative loan disbursements with the Business Office Oversee and complete verification for all undergraduate students Counsel student and parents on all financial aid programs and application requirements Complete Pell Reconciliation with the Business Office Counsel students and parents by phone and in person about financial aid and bills Attend conferences, presentations and seminars for professional development and stay current with new rules and regulations Other duties as assigned Marginal Functions Opening the mail Filing Assisting with mailings Helping other staff when needed Answering finaid@presby.edu emails Expectation As part of Outrageous service initiatives, staff will create communication flow with families and respond to all emails and phone calls within 24 hours. Experience and Education Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university or equivalent experience Three to five years of experience in higher education setting preferred Excellent interpersonal, verbal and written skills Working knowledge of Banner tools desired Basic mathematical skills and ability to perform mathematical computations accurately. Maintain confidentiality Effective oral and written communications to maintain cooperative working relationships with persons contacted in the course of performing assigned duties Working knowledge of Microsoft Office products Demonstrate ability to follow through with projects and meet given deadlines Ability to establish and maintain rapport with prospective students and families, current student body and parents, faculty and staff Ability to manage multiple projects with time sensitive deadlines while maintaining excellent, personalized financial aid service to parents, students, faculty and staff Ability to diffuse difficult or emotional situations with students and/or parents To Apply Please submit application materials—CV/Resume, cover letter, and list of three references to hr@presby.edu . Presbyterian College is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to creating and sustaining an environment in which all individuals are treated with respect and dignity. The College does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, creed, national or ethnic origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, disability, veteran status, or any other legally protected status. Learn More About PC About PC History, Mission, & Plan Benefits & Resources Resources For Close Menu Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends First-Gen Students Community Search for: 503 South Broad Street Clinton, South Carolina 29325 800.476.7272 Contact Us facebook instagram x flickr Quick Links & Resources Quick Links & Resources News Events Directory Athletics Campus Map Living on Campus Academic Calendar Course Catalog Offices & Facilities Accreditation Job Opportunities Justice & Community Wellbeing First-Gen Students International Students Accessible Education Health & Wellness Single-Sign On BannerWeb Brightspace Campus Bookstore Library Online Payment Resources For Close Menu Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends First-Gen Students Community Search for: © Copyright 2026 Presbyterian College | Title IX Policies Consumer Information Campus Police Presbyterian College is committed to providing an accessible and inclusive online experience. If you are unable to access any part of this website due to a disability, please contact Accessible Education at accommodations@presby.edu for assistance. NOTICE OF NONDISCRIMINATORY POLICY AS TO STUDENTS: Presbyterian College is an equal educational opportunity institution. The College’s admission standards and practices are free from discrimination on the basis of age, sex, race, creed, color, disability, ethnicity or national origin. Apply Info Visit Give Search for: Resources For Close Menu Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends First-Gen Students Community English Spanish en"
